  {
    "equipment_id": "681",
    "equipment_eq_id": "EQ ID 681",
    "equipment_name": "Banding Shredder",
    "department": "Maintenance",
    "wo_id": "11742",
    "audit_item": "Disconnect power & \n1) Knife removal & rotation\n- Remove feed works guard assembly, then remove 4 bolts holding feed works in place\n- Begin swinging the feed works open. The chain connecting the feed works to the gear reducer can be slipped off once of the sprockets.\n- Pivot feed works assembly clear. Remove the infeed material guide by removing 4 button head screws. Both knifes can be accessed through opening in front housing, you may have to rotate flywheel by hand to bring knife to access hole.\n- Remove bolts securing knifes. If there is a shim in knife pocket, leave in place when rotating knife edge.\n- Clean knife pockets thoroughly and move any burrs on the used knife edge to assure it is set properly.\n- Replace knife in pocket and lightly tighten bolts. Seat knife by tapping it with brass hammer.\n-Finish tightening the bolts with a torque wrench (60 ft-lb)",
